      {
        "id": 19,
        "payload": {
          "text": "## Section 5: Prohibited Items\n\nThe following items are NOT reimbursable under the meal expense policy:\n\n### Section 5.1: Alcohol on Personal Claims\nAlcoholic beverages are NOT reimbursable for individual meals. Alcohol may be approved for business entertainment meals (Section 3) with advance approval and written justification.\n\n### Section 5.2: Tobacco Products\nCigarettes, cigars, vaping products, and all tobacco-related items are strictly non-reimbursable.\n\n### Section 5.3: Personal Groceries\nGroceries, meal kits, or food items purchased for home consumption are not eligible, even during business travel. Only restaurant or prepared meal receipts qualify.\n\n### Section 5.4: Minibar and In-Room Dining\nHotel minibar charges and in-room dining are NOT reimbursable unless pre-approved for exceptional circumstances (e.g., mandatory quarantine, medical restriction).\n\n### Section 5.5: Non-Meal Items\nPurchases of non-food items on the same receipt (e.g., toiletries, magazines, gifts) must be excluded from the claimed amount. Submit itemized receipt with non-meal items clearly marked as excluded.",
          "file": "meals.md",
          "category": "meals",
          "section": "Section 5: Prohibited Items"
        },
