      {
        "id": 20,
        "payload": {
          "text": "## Section 6: Required Documentation\n\nAll meal expense claims must be submitted with the following documentation:\n\n### Section 6.1: Original Receipt\nOriginal receipt (physical or electronic) showing:\n- Merchant name and location\n- Date and time of purchase\n- Itemized list of food and beverages (required for claims above SGD 30)\n- Payment method and total amount\n\nCredit card statements are NOT acceptable as primary documentation.\n\n### Section 6.2: Receipt Retention\nRetain original receipts for 7 years in accordance with university financial record-keeping policy. Digital scans or photos must be clear and legible.\n\n### Section 6.3: Lost Receipt Affidavit\nFor lost receipts, submit Lost Receipt Affidavit (LRA-02) with the following:\n- Written explanation of loss circumstances\n- Estimated meal cost and date\n- Credit card or bank statement showing the transaction\n- Manager approval\n\nLost receipt claims are limited to **2 per fiscal year** per employee.\n\n### Section 6.4: Group Meal Documentation\nFor group meals (2 or more SUTD employees), submit:\n- Single receipt with total amount\n- List of all attendees with employee IDs\n- Reimbursement split among attendees (per-person breakdown)\n\nEach attendee's individual claim must not exceed their daily cap (Section 2.4).\n\n---\n\n**Policy Effective Date:** January 1, 2026\n**Last Revised:** January 1, 2026\n**Policy Owner:** SUTD Finance Department\n**Review Cycle:** Annual",
          "file": "meals.md",
          "category": "meals",
          "section": "Section 6: Required Documentation"
        },
